<header><p class="enc-kicker">State</p><h1 class="enc-title">Kingdom of Zimbabwe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Kingdom of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwe">Zimbabwe</a> was the state centred on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/great-zimbabwe">Great Zimbabwe</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zimbabwean-plateau">Zimbabwe plateau</a>, which flourished from about the twelfth to the fifteenth century. Its stone enclosures and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gold-trade">gold trade</a> with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/swahili">Swahili</a> coast made it a major southern African power. Its decline was followed by the rise of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mutapa-empire">Mutapa Empire</a>, which inherited much of its political and commercial tradition.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/kingdom-of-zimbabwe.jpg" alt="Kingdom of Zimbabwe" width="320" height="407" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Cefala_Manich_Simbaoe.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
